<title>THAILAND: Thai agency sees steady to higher 1997 growth.</title>
<headline>Thai agency sees steady to higher 1997 growth.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private economic think tank Thailand Development Research Institute (TDRI) on Tuesday said it expects the Thai economy to grow in a 6.0-7.1 percent range in 1997 against its 6.1 percent projection for this year.</p>
<p>TDRI released the following projected economic indicators for 1996 and 1997:</p>
<p>					1995     1996	     1997</p>
<p>								 High     Low</p>
<p> GDP				   8.8	6.1	 7.1     6.0</p>
<p> Inflation			   5.8	5.6	 4.9     4.5</p>
<p> Export growth (%)		23.6	3.9	11.5     5.5</p>
<p> Import growth (%)		30.5	7.5	12.6     7.5</p>
<p> Trade deficit (% of GDP)     -9.1     -9.9     -10.2   -10.1</p>
<p>Current account</p>
<p>  deficit (% of GDP)	    -8.2     -8.8	-9.2    -9.0</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662)-2529950-3 REUTER VA</p>
</text>
